<div class="article-detail-page">
    <div class="article-body">

        <p>If something unexpected comes up, you can request a cancellation before the seller ships your order. The seller reviews your request and decides whether to approve it. In limited cases, Lively may step in to help.</p>

        <p>If your cancellation is approved, your order will be canceled and fully refunded. If it's declined — or the seller doesn't respond within 48 hours — your order will ship as normal.</p>

        <p><strong>Note:</strong> All bids are binding under our <a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">Community Guidelines</a>. When you win an auction, you're expected to complete the purchase. If something unexpected happens, you can still request a cancellation.</p>

        <p>Every purchase is backed by our <a asp-action="ProtectionPolicy">Buyer Protection Policy</a>. We're here to help make things right.</p>

        <p><strong>In this article:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="#when-you-can-request">When you can request cancellation</a></li>
            <li><a href="#how-to-request">How to request cancellation</a></li>
            <li><a href="#what-happens-after">What happens after you request cancellation</a></li>
            <li><a href="#when-lively-steps-in">When Lively may step in</a></li>
            <li><a href="#faqs">Frequently asked questions (FAQs)</a></li>
        </ul>

        <hr />

        <h2 id="when-you-can-request">When you can request cancellation</h2>

        <p>You can ask the seller to cancel your purchase if:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>They haven't created a shipping label yet, or</li>
            <li>It's been less than 24 hours since you placed the order (even if a label was created).</li>
        </ul>

        <p>If you need support, you can still <a asp-action="GetHelpWithPurchase">get help with your purchase</a>.</p>

        <p><strong>Note:</strong> Trust is core to the Lively community. Frequent cancellations may lead to <a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">account action</a> under our <a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">Community Guidelines</a>.</p>

        <h2 id="how-to-request">How to request cancellation</h2>

        <p>You can request cancellation for individual items in an order.</p>

        <p>If an item is part of a bundle, only that item will be canceled and refunded, including its portion of shipping. The rest of the bundle will remain unless you request cancellation for those items too.</p>

