        <h2 id="what-happens-after">What happens after you request cancellation</h2>

        <p>Your order status will change to <strong>Pending Cancellation</strong>, and your request will be sent to the seller.</p>

        <p>The seller has 48 hours to respond:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>If approved:</strong> Your order is canceled and refunded to your original payment method within 3–5 business days.</li>
            <li><strong>If declined or no response within 48 hours:</strong> The order remains final and will ship as normal.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>You'll be notified as soon as the seller responds.</p>

        <div class="article-info-box">
            <strong>Tip:</strong> Check your order status anytime under <strong>Activity &gt; Purchases.</strong>
        </div>

        <h2 id="when-lively-steps-in">When Lively may step in</h2>

        <p>Most cancellation requests are handled by the seller. In certain situations, Lively may help or make limited exceptions:</p>

        <ul>
            <li><strong>Bidding error (auction purchases only):</strong> If you experienced a technical issue while bidding, <a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">contact Support</a> within 2 hours. Include details and screenshots, if available.</li>
            <li><strong>One-time exception:</strong> If a shipping label hasn't been created and you haven't received an exception before, Lively may approve a one-time cancellation for eligible buyers. This doesn't apply to Card Breaks or items that can be used or consumed on-screen.</li>
            <li><strong>EU or UK buyers:</strong> You may have cancellation rights under local consumer laws. Review our <a asp-action="ProtectionPolicy">Buyer Protection Policy</a> for details on the EU/UK Right of Withdrawal.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Cancellations and refunds aren't offered for buyer's remorse, and Lively reserves the right to deny requests. Learn more in our <a asp-action="ProtectionPolicy">Buyer Protection Policy</a>.</p>

        <h2 id="faqs">Frequently asked questions (FAQs)</h2>

        <h3>I bid by mistake and won. Can I cancel?</h3>
        <p>You can <a asp-action="RequestToCancelOrder">request cancellation</a> for the seller to review, but approval isn't guaranteed.</p>

        <h3>Can I cancel my pre-bid?</h3>
        <p>No. Pre-bids can't be canceled or changed. <a asp-action="PreBid">Learn more.</a></p>

        <h3>My package is delayed. Can I cancel my order?</h3>
        <p>Orders can't be canceled once they're in transit. <a asp-action="GetHelpWithPurchase">Learn what to do if your package is delayed.</a></p>

